# Dependencies
# No trailing slash, deliberately. `node_modules/` matches only a DIRECTORY, so a
# SYMLINK named node_modules (the usual git-worktree trick for sharing one install
# across worktrees) is not matched and `git add -A` sweeps it straight in — which
# is exactly how an absolute-path symlink reached a commit on 2026-08-10.
node_modules
.pnp
.pnp.js

# Testing
coverage/
coverage-db/

# Next.js
.next/
out/

# Production
build/

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# Debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Local env files
#
# NOTE: `.github` was listed here until 2026-08-29 and did not belong — it is a
# CI directory, not a local env file. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` was already
# tracked so it was unaffected, but any NEW file added there was silently
# unstageable, which is exactly the trap someone restoring the GitHub mirror
# workflow would have hit. `.claude` is narrowed to its worktrees dir for the
# same reason: agent worktrees are disposable, agent config is not.
.claude/worktrees/
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local

# Vercel
.vercel

# TypeScript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Database
prisma/dev.db
prisma/dev.db-journal
.superpowers/
